<title>UK: UK blocks French bid for MidKent water co.</title>
<headline>UK blocks French bid for MidKent water co.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Trade and Industry said on Monday it had decided to prohibit a proposed bid by General Utilities plc and SAUR Water Services plc, both local units of larger French groups, from making a proposed bid for small water company Mid Kent Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>In a detailed statement, the minister Ian Lang said he agreed with the Monopolies and Mergers Commission's report which concluded that such a merger would be against the public interest.</p>
<p>General Utilities is part of Generale des Eaux while Saur is a unit of construction group Bouygues.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
